    "diagnosis": "Different types of cytological samples",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A</strong>&nbsp;Direct smears (with/without microdissection/macrodissection). Pap-stained and Giemsa-stained and/or unstained slides. Cell scraping preferred. <strong>B</strong>&nbsp;Needle-rinse, supernatant, and fresh samples. <strong>A</strong>&nbsp;and <strong>B</strong>&nbsp;give high-quality DNA/RNA. <strong>C</strong>&nbsp;Optimal quality for extraction of DNA/RNA. <strong>D</strong>&nbsp;Cell blocks; long formalin fixation can lead to C&gt;T or G&gt;A artefacts.",
