  {
    "pkattachmentId": 46162,
    "bookid": 48,
    "chapterId": 122,
    "fileId": 24273,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Molecular testing of cytological specimens</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "María D. Lozano",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<div class=\"WordSection1\">\r\n<table class=\"MsoTableGrid\" style=\"width: 703.8pt; border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"938\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Basic terminology</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.9pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Definition</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 399.0pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"532\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Testing recommendation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 89.15pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 89.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Analytical threshold</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 89.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Minimal input requirement for successful testing as determined by laboratory validation (LOD)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 399.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 89.15pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"532\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Analytical performance of an assay is measured by its accuracy, precision, analytical specificity, and analytical sensitivity (LOD); establishment of the LOD is critical for sequencing assays used to detect the presence of low-frequency variants (SNVs, indels) and is defined as the lowest allelic frequency at which the mutant alleles can be consistently detected in &ge;&nbsp;95% of the test cases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 17.45pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.45pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Preanalytics</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.45pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Collection, processing, and handling of specimens</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 399.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 17.45pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"532\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Specimens must be of sufficient quality to be successfully analysed by molecular testing methods</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Tumour fraction (T%) or neoplastic cell fraction</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Percentage of tumour/neoplastic cell nuclei in a sample (total number of tumour/neoplastic cell nuclei relative to total number of all nucleated cells)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 399.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"532\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">For NGS:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">1. T% &ge;&nbsp;20: reliable NGS readout</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">2. T% &lt;&nbsp;20: use one of the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.05pt;\">a. single-target mutation analysis of high sensitivity (PCR-based methods such as Droplet Digital PCR)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.05pt;\">b. NGS testing with enrichment of tumour cells (laser microdissection)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"margin-left: 14.05pt;\">c. NGS with molecular barcodes that label each original DNA fragment within the sample and thereby increase analytical sensitivity and specificity</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 135.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"181\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>Input DNA/RNA</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 168.9pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"225\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Minimum amount of DNA/RNA to obtain valid results</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 399.0pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"532\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Nucleic acid input for NGS testing depends on the assay and platform used, gene panel size, target enrichment method, and DNA quality</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">LOD, lowest limit of detection; NGS, next-generation sequencing.</p>\r\n</div>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 46167,
    "bookid": 48,
    "chapterId": 122,
    "fileId": 29404,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p>Commonly used testing methodologies for guideline-recommended molecular targets in non-small cell lung carcinoma</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Sinchita Roy-Chowdhuri",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoNormalTable\" style=\"width: 694.6pt; border-collapse: collapse;\" border=\"0\" width=\"926\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Molecular alteration</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Commonly used testing methodology</span></strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 179.05pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 179.05pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>EGFR</em> mutations</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Most common (~90%) <em>EGFR</em> sensitizing mutations include exon&nbsp;19 deletion and p.L858R point mutation in exon&nbsp;21; predictive of response to EGFR TKIs</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Exon&nbsp;20 mutations (usually insertions) are heterogeneous, with a subset that respond to TKI therapy and therefore require knowledge of specific mutation</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><em>EGFR</em> p.T790M mutation is the most common resistance mechanism to first- and second-generation TKI therapy, detection of which warrants switching to third-generation TKIs</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 179.05pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Sanger sequencing with tumour enrichment</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Real-time PCR</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Next-generation sequencing</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 81.55pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 81.55pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"color: black;\">ALK</span></em><span style=\"color: black;\"> rearrangements</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Most common fusion partner is <em>EML4</em>, but variety of fusion partners identified</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Predictive of response to ALK TKIs</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 81.55pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">FISH using break-apart probes</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Immunochemistry (D5F3 clone; 5A4 clone); may be used as a standalone test without confirmation</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Next-generation sequencing</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid; height: 66.1pt;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 66.1pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>ROS1</em> rearrangements</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variety of fusion partners identified including <em>CD74</em>, <em>SLC34A2</em>, <em>CCDC6</em>, <em>GOPC</em> (<em>FIG</em>)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Predictive of response to ROS1 TKIs</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; height: 66.1pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>FISH using break-apart probes</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Immunochemistry (D4D6 clone); can be used as screening, but if positive requires confirmation by molecular test</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Next-generation sequencing</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"color: black;\">BRAF</span></em><span style=\"color: black;\"> p.V600E mutations</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Activating mutations result in unregulated MAPK/ERK signalling</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Predictive of response to combined therapy using BRAF and MEK inhibitors</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Real-time PCR</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Sanger sequencing with tumour enrichment</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Next-generation sequencing</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">BRAF p.V600E antibody for immunochemistry not extensively validated</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>MET</em> exon&nbsp;14&ndash;skipping mutations</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Predictive of response to MET TKIs</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Next-generation sequencing</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"color: black;\">KRAS</span></em><span style=\"color: black;\"> p.G12C mutations</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Most commonly involving mutations in codon&nbsp;12</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Previously prognostic, but recently p.G12C mutations targetable</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Real-time PCR</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Sanger sequencing with tumour enrichment</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Next-generation sequencing</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>RET</em> rearrangements</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Variety of fusion partners identified, including <em>KIF5B</em>, <em>CCDC6</em>, <em>NCOA4</em></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Predictive of response to oral RET TKIs</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>FISH using break-apart probes; sensitivity dependent on fusion partner (low sensitivity for <em>NCOA4</em>::<em>RET</em>)</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Targeted real-time reverse transcriptase PCR; may not detect novel partners</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Next-generation sequencing</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em><span style=\"color: black;\">NTRK1/2/3</span></em><span style=\"color: black;\"> fusions</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Variety of fusion partners identified</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">FISH: requires three separate probe sets</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Immunochemistry: high sensitivity, but may have underlying baseline expression in some tissues</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span><span style=\"color: black;\">Next-generation sequencing </span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">PDL1</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Expressed in tumour cells and inhibits T&nbsp;cell&ndash;mediated cell death</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>High PDL1 expression predictive of response to checkpoint inhibitor therapy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 347.3pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"463\">\r\n<p class=\"TableBullet\" style=\"tab-stops: 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt 'Times New Roman';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span>Immunohistochemistry using PDL1 antibody clones (please refer to <span class=\"ID-Section\"><span style=\"color: black;\">&lt;&lt;3.2.0.1&gt;&gt;</span></span><em>Immunocytochemistry</em><span class=\"PageCh\"><span style=\"color: black;\">, p.&nbsp;XXX</span></span>)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">TKI, tyrosine kinase inhibitor.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]